 in [47001,48000] and one in [51001,53000] (step_07, step_09, step_11). For a <=600-unit-gap cascade the only temporally plausible branch is 303's first event at ~47.0-47.5k. That event is not to 1583 or 1465 (step_12, step_13), hence it is 303->1409; 1409's only outgoing contact in the following ~600+ units is to 960, not toward 1293 or its in-neighbours (step_16). The 1293 in-event in [47001,48000] came from 1574, not from 28 or 1438 (step_14, step_15), i.e. from an unrelated source. 1293's later in-event (51001-53000) precedes 303's second event, and no 1293 in-events exist after 56000, so 303's later events cannot reach it. Although 303 and 1293 are connected in the time-ignoring 2-hop/3-hop neighbourhood via the hub node 28 and the dense graph of 8124 events (step_01, step_03), no chain of interactions with successive gaps <=600 links 303 to 1293. The static connectivity is a hub artefact, not a temporal cascade.", "confidence": 0.72, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}]}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_ff72bb61\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [303, 1293],\n  \"window\": [28296, 66695],\n  \"narrative\": \"Node 303 is very sparsely active in the window: only 3 outgoing events (step_02, step_04), localized by binary-search windowing to ~[47001,47500], ~[53001,56000] and ~[63001,66695] (step_06, step_08, step_10). Node 1293 receives only 5 events, from {28, 1438, 1574} (step_02, step_05), localized to ~[28296,38000], two in [42001,47000], one in [47001,48000] and one in [51001,53000] (step_07, step_09, step_11). For a <=600-unit-gap cascade the only temporally plausible branch is 303's first event at ~47.0-47.5k. That event is not to 1583 or 1465 (step_12, step_13), hence it is 303->1409; 1409's only outgoing contact in the following ~600+ units is to 960, not toward 1293 or its in-neighbours (step_16). The 1293 in-event in [47001,48000] came from 1574, not from 28 or 1438 (step_14, step_15), i.e. from an unrelated source. 1293's later in-event (51001-53000) precedes 303's second event, and no 1293 in-events exist after 56000, so 303's later events cannot reach it. Although 303 and 1293 are connected in the time-ignoring 2-hop/3-hop neighbourhood via the hub node 28 and the dense graph of 8124 events (step_01, step_03), no chain of interactions with successive gaps <=600 links 303 to 1293. The static connectivity is a hub artefact, not a temporal cascade.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.72,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"rol